WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:06.683
Journey ten: list a business. A member describes a business and submits

00:00:06.683 --> 00:00:11.186
it for verification. This run finishes what was left.

00:00:12.091 --> 00:00:16.681
The form now has a highlight, a short green line on the card.

00:00:16.681 --> 00:00:20.443
The preview draws it, marked Pending verification.

00:00:21.795 --> 00:00:26.897
Add a service opens the full service editor, with what members can do:

00:00:26.897 --> 00:00:31.707
book a time, or ask for a quote. The service stays with the draft.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:40.033
The verification team's review says No products or services yet, and

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:44.130
names the owner's other listings and drafts, with their stages.

00:00:45.256 --> 00:00:50.203
When the statement of faith is updated, an owner is asked the next time

00:00:50.203 --> 00:00:52.921
they open the app, and has thirty days.

00:00:52.921 --> 00:00:56.056
Not now leaves Read and agree on My business.

00:00:56.761 --> 00:01:01.057
I agree records the agreement with its version, and thanks them.

00:01:02.157 --> 00:01:06.295
After thirty days, the daily job pauses the listing.

00:01:06.295 --> 00:01:12.025
Nothing is deleted. Read and agree replaces Resume listing, and agreeing

00:01:12.025 --> 00:01:14.253
makes it live again at once.

00:01:15.137 --> 00:01:20.540
Behind the screen, both daily jobs run once, however many workers run,

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:25.711
and record their last success. A submission slower than ten seconds

00:01:25.711 --> 00:01:29.801
fails rather than spinning. The tests prove each one.

00:01:30.663 --> 00:01:35.989
Journey ten is complete. Comparing the new screens with their mocks is

00:01:35.989 --> 00:01:37.359
left to the owner.
